N. Provide sound design and feedback specification

Include ball release, seam movement, pitch bounce by length, bat sweet spot, edges, toe, pad, stumps, bails, keeper gloves, catch, pickup, throw, running, slide, crowd, umpire and UI cues. Specify restrained mobile haptics and audio mixing priorities.

O. Define game balance and telemetry

Specify what should be measured: shot success by line/length, timing distribution, contact types, boundaries, wickets, catches, run-outs, delivery variation use, latency, reconnect and performance. Define balance metrics and guard against hidden outcome manipulation. Player skill ratings may influence execution precision modestly, but human decision and execution must dominate.

